Do you ever dream of WoW?

Imagine the scene: the boss has been defeated, and after five
grueling
hours you're finally able to step out of the instance victorious. You
log out to catch some shut eye, and your mind fills with images of
the
mobs you've just defeated. You're now dreaming of WoW.
A forum post about this subject really got me thinking. In fact,
evidently even Eyonix dreams of WoW, which I guess isn't all that
surprising really. I often dream that I am in game when I am happily
zonked out. For me, I think it is a case of sensory input; I dream a
lot of times about what I see and hear. A while back I prepared the
night before a business meeting by printing out my reports and
leaving
them by the door so that I wouldn't forget them. I didn't, but in my
dreams that night I did. The same is true of World of Warcraft. I
spent so much time immersed in the game that it sometimes slips into
my dreams as well.


Do you dream of WoW? What sorts of in game elements slip into your
slumber?


